{
  "name": "New post to IndexNow (Bing, Yandex and partners)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## New post to IndexNow (Bing, Yandex and partners)\n\n**What it does**\nWhen you publish a post, this tells Bing, Yandex and the other IndexNow search engines about the URL within minutes, instead of waiting for their crawlers. Works from your RSS feed or from a webhook your CMS calls. Every submission is logged to Google Sheets with the response code.\n\n**You need**\nAn IndexNow key file on your site (README explains, 2 minutes), and a Google Sheets credential for the log.\n\n**Setup**\n1. Create your key and upload `<key>.txt` to your site root.\n2. Put the key and your host in **Build the IndexNow request**, your feed URL in **New post in RSS feed** and your sheet ID in **Log the submission**.\n3. Run once with a real post URL, then activate.\n\nBuilt by AI Strike Force, aistrikeforce.com",
        "height": 700,
        "width": 520
      },
      "id": "939adf91-6d62-43a5-a77a-33402c6780ea",
      "name": "New post to IndexNow (Bing, Yandex and partners)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -600,
        40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Edit me\n`KEY`: your IndexNow key.\n`ALLOWED_HOSTS`: your site host(s), for example `www.example.com`. URLs on other hosts are ignored.",
        "height": 280,
        "width": 220,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "52ebf3c2-a48f-429e-a446-b090aaf1e26b",
      "name": "Edit me: key and host",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        180,
        -40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Edit me\nYour RSS or Atom feed URL. Delete this trigger if you only use the webhook.",
        "height": 160,
        "width": 200,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "2235d035-cd58-432a-aabf-525e15610268",
      "name": "Edit me: feed",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -100
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "pollTimes": {
          "item": [
            {
              "mode": "everyHour"
            }
          ]
        },
        "feedUrl": "https://www.example.com/feed.xml"
      },
      "id": "9e7abf26-0d81-4da0-a9a4-112a2bce2979",
      "name": "New post in RSS feed",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.rssFeedReadTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "indexnow-submit",
        "responseMode": "onReceived",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "97b6a194-fa81-4161-a04f-c501372e9e1c",
      "name": "Or: ping from your CMS",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [
        0,
        440
      ],
      "webhookId": "592c1d61-553b-4e20-b099-764b76e48c99"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Your IndexNow key: 8 to 128 characters, letters, numbers and dashes only.\n// The file https://<host>/<KEY>.txt must exist and contain exactly this key.\nconst KEY = 'YOUR_INDEXNOW_KEY';\nconst ALLOWED_HOSTS = ['www.example.com'];\n\n// Collect URLs from either trigger:\n//   RSS item:      { link: 'https://...' }\n//   Webhook body:  { \"url\": \"https://...\" }  or  { \"urls\": [\"https://...\", \"...\"] }\nconst urls = [];\nfor (const { json } of $input.all()) {\n  if (json.link) urls.push(json.link);\n  const body = json.body || {};\n  if (body.url) urls.push(body.url);\n  if (Array.isArray(body.urls)) urls.push(...body.urls);\n}\n\n// Group by host, drop duplicates and anything not on your site.\nconst byHost = {};\nfor (const raw of urls) {\n  let u;\n  try { u = new URL(String(raw).trim()); } catch { continue; }\n  if (!ALLOWED_HOSTS.includes(u.host)) continue;\n  (byHost[u.host] ??= new Set()).add(u.href);\n}\n\nreturn Object.entries(byHost).map(([host, set]) => {\n  const urlList = [...set].slice(0, 10000); // IndexNow accepts up to 10,000 URLs per request\n  return {\n    json: {\n      host,\n      urlList,\n      payload: { host, key: KEY, keyLocation: `https://${host}/${KEY}.txt`, urlList },\n    },\n  };\n});"
      },
      "id": "039bfac4-e190-4fbe-a868-323905f4602d",
      "name": "Build the IndexNow request",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        220,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
